WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:06.470
Napoleon Dynamite was one of the most unlikely
hits of 2004… or any other year, really.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:11.700
Directed by 25-year-old Jared Hess and starring
a cast of mostly unknowns, the quirky indie

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:18.580
comedy was difficult to categorize, and against
all odds, it grossed $44 million against a

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.580
$400,000 budget.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:27.580
So, why won't Hollywood make a Napoleon Dynamite
sequel?

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.609
Too busy hunting wolverines

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:34.089
Napoleon Dynamite led to a brief but fruitful
period for star Jon Heder.

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:38.609
He starred in a string of comedies that included
Just Like Heaven, The Benchwarmers, and Blades

00:00:38.609 --> 00:00:39.609
of Glory.

00:00:39.609 --> 00:00:44.710
Heder has since switched gears, putting his
distinctive cadence to use as a voice actor.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.899
"Hello."

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:50.249
He's racked up more than a dozen credits for
work on animated movies, TV cartoons, and

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:51.249
video games.

00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:54.769
Also a major time-suck for Heder: the man
has a whole mess of kids.

00:00:54.769 --> 00:00:58.809
And while director Jared Hess can't seem to
find much support for his own films, he's

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:01.449
still a director in demand for other folks'
projects.

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:06.610
He's helmed a few movies written by people
other than himself or his wife, like the 2016

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:11.080
comedy Masterminds, and is slated to direct
the next, long-awaited entry in Jackie Chan's

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.230
comedic Shanghai Trilogy.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.390
Studios only want directors with skills

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.550
Even still, Jared and Jerusha Hess have continued
to make one-of-a-kind movies in their own

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:20.590
style and flavor.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.790
But they just don't put butts in seats.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:27.750
Among their efforts: the luchador comedy Nacho
Libre, the fantasy fiction send-up Gentlemen

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.750
Broncos, and the caper comedy Don Verdean.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.270
The directors have a unique vision, but they've
had a hard time attracting sizable audiences.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:41.390
Case in point: Gentlemen Broncos grossed just
$113,000, which is about three times as much

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.940
as Don Verdean pulled in.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:47.530
And that's despite both films having the comedy
star power of fan favorites Sam Rockwell and

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:52.020
Jemaine Clement.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.070
The director doesn't flippin' feel like it

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:58.550
Napoleon Dynamite is a classic example of
lightning in a bottle, which nobody understands

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:02.870
better than Jared Hess, so he doesn't even
really want to try making a sequel.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:07.520
In 2010, he told Star Pulse that because the
movie was conceived as a one-time deal, a

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.359
sequel wouldn't work, saying,

00:02:09.359 --> 00:02:13.480
"When sequels are an afterthought, they usually
end up being bad, but when they were originally

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.480
intended to have multiple films made up of
the same story, I think it works."

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.480
In other words,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.870
"What are you going to do today, Napoleon?"

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.420
"Whatever I feel like I wanna do GOSH!"

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.680
The cartoon bombed

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.441
Eight years after its auspicious big-screen
debut, Napoleon Dynamite did get a sequel

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:31.879
of sorts: an animated TV series.

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:37.040
Six episodes ran on Fox in the spring of 2012,
and the entire main cast reprised their original

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.040
roles.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.629
The show finished the 2011-12 season at #103
in the ratings…after which it was quietly

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:44.629
canceled.

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:45.629
"Dang it!

00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:47.180
You guys are idiots!"

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.709
Napoleon lives on

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:53.209
Audiences were able to pay another unofficial
visit to Napoleon Dynamite's universe courtesy

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:56.970
of an ad campaign that aired shortly after
the film's theatrical run.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:03.889
"In days of yore, the Utah state fair didn't
have sweet rides, like the Scrambler, Rock-o

00:03:03.889 --> 00:03:06.180
Plane, The Octopus…"

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:11.079
Jon Heder and Efren Ramirez reprised their
characters a few more times in a series of

00:03:11.079 --> 00:03:15.349
TV spots promoting the 2005 Utah State Fair.

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:16.639
Also making a cameo?

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:17.639
Delicious tots.

00:03:17.639 --> 00:03:19.230
"That Kangaroo looks pretty good."

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.000
"It's a Totzilla, and it should look good,
I baked my butt off."

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.870
Never has a fictional character loved the
potato nuggets as much as Napoleon.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:32.019
The movie is so connected with tater tots
that in 2016, Burger King recruited Heder

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:36.629
and Ramirez to star in a commercial for the
chain's latest offering, Cheesy Tots.

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:37.669
It's too late

00:03:37.669 --> 00:03:41.790
Napoleon Dynamite is pretty much a high school
movie, and following the film's characters

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:46.329
as they all tackle college and marriage just
doesn't seem like it would be a very rewarding

00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:47.329
project.

00:03:47.329 --> 00:03:50.370
And if all of the characters are all still
somehow living in the same small town that

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.989
never escaped the late '80s, wandering ever-closer
to death, well, the audience has already seen

00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:56.459
how they behave in that environment.

00:03:56.459 --> 00:04:01.109
There's just not a lot more to say, and watching
Napoleon slowly lose his trademark cloud of

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:02.620
hair to old age just seems depressing.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.010
At least we'll always have the original.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.120
"Always and forever.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.140
Always and forever..."

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:11.340
Thanks for watching!

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.999
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:16.450
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

